Yes, but it is not recommended.

Example:

<Typewriter

words={[
"Hello, I am Anand. I am a Full Stack Developer."
]}

/>

It will type the complete paragraph:

Hello,
I am Anand.
I am a Full Stack Developer.

But for paragraphs:

Better use:

Fade animation
Scroll animation
AOS
Framer Motion

Typewriter is best for:

Short Text
Titles
Headings
Keywords
Roles 10. Why use Typewriter Library Instead of useEffect?

Without library:

You need to manage:

state
↓
current text
↓
character index
↓
typing speed
↓
deleting logic
↓
loop logic
↓
timer cleanup

Example:

useEffect(()=>{

const timer=setInterval(()=>{

// change text

},200)

return()=>{
clearInterval(timer)
}

},[])

Library automatically handles everything.

11. Typewriter Working Flow

Internally it works like this:

Component Render
|
↓
Read words array
|
↓
Start typing first word
|
↓
Complete word
|
↓
Wait delaySpeed
|
↓
Delete word
|
↓
Move to next word
|
↓
Repeat if loop=true 12. Important Props Summary
Prop Purpose
words Text list to display
loop Repeat animation
cursor Show cursor
cursorStyle Cursor symbol
typeSpeed Typing speed
deleteSpeed Removing speed
delaySpeed Waiting time
onLoopDone Function after loop complete
onType Runs while typing
onDelete Runs while deleting
